    {
      "id": "evidence-003-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "This is what makes the generalization a STRENGTHENING rather than a different claim: the old statement is a corollary, obtained by instantiation, and the kernel re-checks the application. Under the tight telescope (only the declarations the proof rests on) the recovered footprint is identical to the original's, name for name; under the full 30-binder interface it is a superset, because the instantiation deliberately mentions ring laws the proof never used. `--require-empty` fails the process if any fixture is not axiom-free or any instantiation does not recover the original.",
